From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] security: include the QButtonGroup definition

The quota editor constructs QButtonGroup and calls addButton, but the
transitive Qt headers only forward-declare that type. Include its definition
in the translation unit that uses it. This does not change quota behavior.

Patch-Source: downstream adaptation of tora 3.2 src/tools/tosecurity.cpp
Patch-License: GPL-2.0-only
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (automated upstream writes forbidden)
Applies-To: tora 3.2
Remove-When: upstream tosecurity.cpp includes QButtonGroup before using it
---
 src/tools/tosecurity.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/tools/tosecurity.cpp b/src/tools/tosecurity.cpp
--- a/src/tools/tosecurity.cpp
+++ b/src/tools/tosecurity.cpp
@@ -47,2 +47,3 @@
 #include <QSplitter>
+#include <QButtonGroup>
 #include <QToolBar>
